{%- comment -%}
  The sims Guido reads, as marks that jump to that sim's tab in "Get started".

  One list for both Guido pages: they open on the same hero and carry the same
  tabs, so the anchors resolve on either one. The marks are stencils painted as
  masks in guido.css, so they take the colour of the label beside them in either
  theme rather than shipping a black PNG that disappears on a dark background.

  Assetto Corsa and Competizione share a mark, the same way the app's sim picker
  shares it: there is no separate Competizione logo, and the label beside the
  mark is what tells the two apart.

  The heading is for screen readers only. The marks and their names say what they
  are on sight, and a visible "Works with" above them was a caption for a picture
  that already had one.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="product-sims">
  <h2 class="ds-sr-only">Supported sims</h2>
  <ul class="product-sims__list">
    {%- for sim in guidoSims.sims %}
      <li>
        <a class="product-sim" href="#sim-{{ sim.id }}">
          <span class="sim-mark sim-mark--{{ sim.mark }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="product-sim__name">{{ sim.name }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
